# SUPABASE SCHEMA SYNC RULE

Imajica will connect to a **dedicated Supabase project** later. Until then, services may use localStorage/demo data — but the **database schema must stay current**.

## When building or changing any feature that stores or loads data

You MUST update Supabase SQL in the same change set:

1. Add or alter tables/columns in a new file under `supabase/migrations/` (timestamped, never rewrite applied history casually).
2. Update `supabase/seed.sql` when demo/default rows are needed.
3. Add or adjust RLS policies for new tables/columns.
4. Match TypeScript types in `src/types` and service field names to SQL (`snake_case` in DB).

## Current feature → table map (keep updated)

| App area | Tables / notes |
|---|---|
| Auth / roles | `profiles` (+ `status`), `user_roles`, `roles` (`BRANCH_ADMIN` description = Clinic Manager), views `v_team_user_access` / `v_user_access_directory`, RPC `set_profile_active` |
| Branches / settings | `branches` (+ `branch_type`), `branch_hours`, `branch_rooms`, `system_settings`; RPC `set_branch_active` |
| Team / recruitment & LMS | `recruitment_applicants`, `lms_courses`, `lms_enrollments` |
| Customer registration & list | `clients` (+ occupation, middle_name, emergency_*, medical_*, avatar_url, admin_notes), `client_skin_profiles`, `client_notes` |
| Client Scheduling | `appointments`, `appointment_status_history` (statuses include `no_show`, `pending`, `completed`, …) |
| Landing Special Offers | `landing_promos` (Marketing admin → landing modal slider) |
| Catalog services & packages | `treatments` (+ sessions, default_branch_id), `packages` (+ free_items, default_branch_id), `package_items`, `branch_treatments` |
| Catalog products / categories / consumables | `inventory_items` (+ category_id), `product_categories`, `consumables` |
| Administration operations | `operational_expenses`, `branch_orders`, `franchise_orders`, `waste_logs`, `warehouse_items` + `warehouse_stock_movements`, `stock_transfers`, `imajica_forms` (+ client_name, form_type, template_file, field_values, signatures) |
| Sales / payments | `sales` (+ `invoice_number`, `payment_type`, `booking_ref`, `referred_by_*`, `doctor_*`, `staff_name`, `lead_source`), `sale_items` (+ `unit_cost`, `sku`), `payments`; `clients.reward_points` |
| Analytics reports | `v_analytics_sales_transactions`, `analytics_sales_summary`, `analytics_product_sales_report`, `analytics_best_selling_treatments`, `analytics_new_client_sales`, `imajica_transaction_fee`; `clients.lead_source` |
| Staff / payroll | `staff` (+ first_name, last_name, birth_date, department, address, avatar_url, emergency_*, `position_id`), `staff_positions` (+ department), `commissions`, `payroll_*`, `plan_b_incentives`; RPC `analytics_staff_sales` (rank by booking_count) |
| Staff attendance | `staff_attendance_logs` (time_in / time_out + selfie + geolocation); storage bucket `attendance-selfies`; `profiles.employee_code`; public RPCs `kiosk_lookup_employee` / `kiosk_attendance_punch` (shared `/timeclock` kiosk) |
| Marketing campaigns | `marketing_campaigns` |
| Inventory | `inventory_items`, `branch_inventory`, `inventory_movements` |

## Do NOT

- Ship a new CRUD/UI data feature with only localStorage and no migration
- Put Imajica tables into another product’s schema without an `imajica`-safe migration plan
- Forget RLS when adding tables readable from the public landing or client portal

## After schema changes

Note in the reply what migration file was added/updated so the user can `supabase db push` or run SQL in the Supabase SQL Editor when the new project is ready.
